The key clue is +20 errors and the enormous baseline RTT. With the candidate link OFF, Ryu may still temporarily believe s2 ↔ s3 exists because our controller handles EventLinkAdd but not EventLinkDelete. That can cause it to select a path through a disabled link until discovery catches up.

So don't interpret this as Braess. In fact, this run shows the candidate link dramatically improving performance, not causing a Braess degradation.

